# Mirrou Creative Studio — Environment Variables
#
# The website is rendered fully static (vite-react-ssg) and served via nginx on
# Cloud Run. It requires NO runtime secrets.
#
# Lead capture: the contact form posts to a FastAPI lead endpoint. That URL is
# intentionally NOT an env var — it is a public, non-secret value baked into the
# static build via `SITE.api` in `src/content/site-data.ts`:
#
#   POST {SITE.api}/api/lead   (currently the Opus-Magnum EU backend, europe-west3)
#
# To point the form at a different backend, change `SITE.api` in site-data.ts
# (single source of truth) and rebuild — do not introduce a runtime secret for it.
#
# Add project-specific variables here only as real integrations are introduced, e.g.:
#   - a consent-gated analytics measurement ID (DSGVO: only AFTER consent)
#
# Never commit real .env files — copy this to .env.local for local overrides.
